      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "In the right triangle $△ABC,$ $∠A$ is a right angle, $AB=3\\sqrt{7},$ $AC=9$ and $BC=12.$ Find $\\operatorname{sin}⁡C.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's illustrate the given triangle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14244094/assets/40f31b56b1078bbab7d423c89088218c3fc52e3a2d56c2170c380d415860c2ad.png)\n\nThe sine of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the hypotenuse (S-O-H). Relative to the angle $C,$ the opposite side is $\\overset{―}{AB},$ and the hypotenuse is $\\overset{―}{CB}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡C & =\\frac{AB}{CB}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{7}}{12}=\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
